WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.266 --> 00:00:02.068
-This is your first time here.
And here we are in New York.

00:00:02.068 --> 00:00:05.605 align:start size:94% position:6%
You're from New Jersey, but we
had as Hollywood a meeting

00:00:05.605 --> 00:00:06.306 size:81% position:41% line:92%
as we could ever have.

00:00:06.306 --> 00:00:10.176
We met and we sat at the same
table at the Golden Globes.

00:00:10.176 --> 00:00:12.812 align:start size:94% position:6%
-It was so Hollywood.
-It was really Hollywood.

00:00:12.812 --> 00:00:14.481 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And we had only been
doing "Brooklyn"

00:00:14.481 --> 00:00:16.016 size:81% position:41% line:92%
for like a few months.

00:00:16.016 --> 00:00:18.018 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And then you guys won.
-And then we won.

00:00:18.018 --> 00:00:20.520 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah. And --
-It was very --

00:00:20.520 --> 00:00:23.123 size:84% position:42% line:92%
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:23.123 --> 00:00:25.125 align:start size:94% position:6%
-That whole night
was so surreal.

00:00:25.125 --> 00:00:28.661 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I remember meeting you
so vividly,

00:00:28.661 --> 00:00:29.429 size:78% position:39% line:92%
because you sat down.

00:00:29.429 --> 00:00:30.463 align:start size:94% position:6%
You were talking to
Chelsea Peretti,

00:00:30.463 --> 00:00:31.865 align:start size:94% position:6%
and I was just like
"It's cool, it's cool.

00:00:31.865 --> 00:00:33.666 align:start size:94% position:6%
It's just Seth Meyers
sitting there.

00:00:33.666 --> 00:00:35.468 size:78% position:39%
Just gonna be part of
this conversation.

00:00:35.468 --> 00:00:37.370 line:92%
Oh, you're talking to me? Okay."

00:00:37.370 --> 00:00:38.571 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-It was really nice.

00:00:38.571 --> 00:00:39.939 line:92%
And then, I will say, you won --

00:00:39.939 --> 00:00:41.107 size:78% position:39%
Because you were very
sweet and nervous,

00:00:41.107 --> 00:00:43.410
and then you won and you came
back and you totally iced me.

00:00:43.410 --> 00:00:44.778 size:88% position:44% line:92%
You changed immediately.

00:00:44.778 --> 00:00:46.880 align:start size:94% position:6%
Like, you were totally
big-timing as soon as you won.

00:00:46.880 --> 00:00:48.681 align:start size:94% position:6%
-That's my move.
-Yeah. That was your move.

00:00:48.681 --> 00:00:50.250 size:81% position:41% line:92%
-That's my move. Yeah.

00:00:50.250 --> 00:00:53.520 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I'm jealous because you
get to work with

00:00:53.520 --> 00:00:54.521 align:start size:94% position:6%
so many wonderful people
on the show,

00:00:54.521 --> 00:00:56.423 align:start size:94% position:6%
but especially Andy Samberg,
one of my old friends.

00:00:56.423 --> 00:00:59.125
How has your experience been
working with Andy Samberg?

00:00:59.125 --> 00:01:01.127
-He's the best.
-He's really the best guy, yeah.

00:01:01.127 --> 00:01:04.764 align:start size:94% position:6%
-He's so nice and wonderful.
It's a little annoying.

00:01:04.764 --> 00:01:10.203 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I think he's also healthier
now, living in L.A.

00:01:10.203 --> 00:01:12.272 align:start size:94% position:6%
and not being on "SNL,"
where we all --

00:01:12.272 --> 00:01:13.773 align:start size:94% position:6%
every one of us
who worked at "SNL"

00:01:13.773 --> 00:01:18.144 align:start size:94% position:6%
was a lot grumpier,
hung over a lot.

00:01:18.144 --> 00:01:21.247 align:start size:94% position:6%
He seems like
green-juiced-out right now.

00:01:21.247 --> 00:01:21.714 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-He is.

00:01:21.714 --> 00:01:23.983 align:start size:94% position:6%
But I really enjoy
when he gets grumpy.

00:01:23.983 --> 00:01:25.018 line:92%
-Yeah, it's pretty funny.

00:01:25.018 --> 00:01:25.819 line:92%
-It happens like once in a while

00:01:25.819 --> 00:01:29.622
and it's very similar, like, how
my 3-year-old gets grumpy.

00:01:29.622 --> 00:01:32.292 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah. This all tracks
with my experience.

00:01:32.292 --> 00:01:36.129 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, yeah.
It's just kind of like...

00:01:36.129 --> 00:01:37.097 line:92%
But, you know, you just, like,

00:01:37.097 --> 00:01:38.832
pour yourself some coffee
and, like, grab a cookie

00:01:38.832 --> 00:01:41.734 size:81% position:41%
and just sit near him,
and he will eventually

00:01:41.734 --> 00:01:44.370 align:start size:94% position:6%
take that coffee
and eat that cookie, like,

00:01:44.370 --> 00:01:45.105 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
from your hands.

00:01:45.105 --> 00:01:48.308 align:start size:94% position:6%
-He does like to be
communal with food...

00:01:48.308 --> 00:01:48.875 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Very much so.

00:01:48.875 --> 00:01:50.710 align:start size:94% position:6%
-...especially when he
doesn't have any.

00:01:50.710 --> 00:01:51.177 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Yes.

00:01:51.177 --> 00:01:54.013 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah. It's not like,
"Have a little of mine."

00:01:54.013 --> 00:01:55.014 line:92%
It's like he doesn't have any.

00:01:55.014 --> 00:01:57.250 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And he's always trying to be
good and healthy

00:01:57.250 --> 00:01:58.051 size:81% position:41% line:92%
so he doesn't get sick

00:01:58.051 --> 00:01:59.552 align:start size:94% position:6%
and, like,
takes care of himself,

00:01:59.552 --> 00:02:01.154 line:92%
so I really enjoy just, like,

00:02:01.154 --> 00:02:02.722 align:start size:94% position:6%
sliding in with
like five cookies.

00:02:02.722 --> 00:02:08.261 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Gotcha. As well you should.
This was very exciting.

00:02:08.261 --> 00:02:09.729 line:92%
There were some people who,

00:02:09.729 --> 00:02:11.698 align:start size:94% position:6%
when the show got
cancelled over at Fox,

00:02:11.698 --> 00:02:15.201 align:start size:94% position:6%
were very vocal
about bringing the show back.

00:02:15.201 --> 00:02:17.837 align:start size:94% position:6%
I was a little vocal,
but one of the people who --

00:02:17.837 --> 00:02:18.605 size:78% position:39% line:92%
-You were very vocal.

00:02:18.605 --> 00:02:19.639 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I was very vocal,
but I will say,

00:02:19.639 --> 00:02:24.244
the star of it, one of the stars
of it, was Lin-Manuel Miranda,

00:02:24.244 --> 00:02:25.178 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
who then...

00:02:25.178 --> 00:02:26.980 size:84% position:42% line:92%
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:26.980 --> 00:02:31.484
His reward was he got to be on
the show and play your brother,

00:02:31.484 --> 00:02:32.719 size:75% position:38% line:92%
which was fantastic.

00:02:32.719 --> 00:02:37.891 align:start size:94% position:6%
How was your experience
with him?

00:02:37.891 --> 00:02:39.492 line:92%
-I have so much love for Lin.

00:02:39.492 --> 00:02:41.227 align:start size:94% position:6%
He tweeted about
the show around, like,

00:02:41.227 --> 00:02:43.796 align:start size:94% position:6%
the Golden Globes time,
early Season 1,

00:02:43.796 --> 00:02:46.699 align:start size:94% position:6%
and I basically ran around set
and I was like,

00:02:46.699 --> 00:02:49.169 align:start size:94% position:6%
"Aah! Lin-Manuel Miranda
loves 'Brooklyn.'"

00:02:49.169 --> 00:02:51.037 align:start size:94% position:6%
Everybody was like, "Who dat?"
-Yeah.

00:02:51.037 --> 00:02:53.473 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Because "Hamilton"
had not come out yet.

00:02:53.473 --> 00:02:56.409 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I was like, "Aah!
Los Angeles!"

00:02:56.409 --> 00:02:59.412 align:start size:94% position:6%
And then "Hamilton" came out,
and everybody was like,

00:02:59.412 --> 00:03:01.814 align:start size:94% position:6%
"Do you know
that Lin-Manuel Miranda

00:03:01.814 --> 00:03:03.383 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
loves 'Brooklyn'?"

00:03:03.383 --> 00:03:04.817 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
I was like...

00:03:04.817 --> 00:03:06.653 align:start size:94% position:6%
So, we've been trying for
a really long time

00:03:06.653 --> 00:03:07.387 size:84% position:42% line:92%
to get him on the show.

00:03:07.387 --> 00:03:10.323 align:start size:94% position:6%
And then through the
whole cancelation, all of --

00:03:10.323 --> 00:03:11.357 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
You, Sean Astin --

00:03:11.357 --> 00:03:13.059 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Sean Astin, who's been on
the show, as well.

00:03:13.059 --> 00:03:14.761 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Who's been on the show.
-Mark Hamill.

00:03:14.761 --> 00:03:15.828 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Mark Hamill.
We got to get him on.

00:03:15.828 --> 00:03:21.034 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Guillermo del Toro.
I was waiting for my call.

00:03:21.034 --> 00:03:22.936 align:start size:94% position:6%
-No, no, no.
You've been on the show.

00:03:22.936 --> 00:03:24.070 line:92%
-Well, I have been on the show.

00:03:24.070 --> 00:03:25.572 line:92%
I will say, you know, this is --

00:03:25.572 --> 00:03:26.906 align:start size:94% position:6%
Like, Lin got to
go out in person

00:03:26.906 --> 00:03:29.809 align:start size:94% position:6%
and, like, wear wardrobe
and have lines.

00:03:29.809 --> 00:03:33.079 align:start size:94% position:6%
My cameo was -- I was
a police sketch on the show.

00:03:33.079 --> 00:03:36.783 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:36.783 --> 00:03:38.084 align:start size:94% position:6%
That counts.
-That counts?

00:03:38.084 --> 00:03:41.688
-Yeah.
-I have to get the prop, though.

00:03:41.688 --> 00:03:43.156 align:start size:94% position:6%
I really do love that
a great deal.

00:03:43.156 --> 00:03:44.057 align:start size:94% position:6%
I'm gonna try to
track that down.

00:03:44.057 --> 00:03:49.062
-Yeah. It kind of looks like
you and Andy had a baby --

00:03:49.062 --> 00:03:51.864 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-That's what that looks like.

00:03:51.864 --> 00:03:54.133 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, we've got
a very similar thing

00:03:54.133 --> 00:03:56.135 align:start size:94% position:6%
that we share in common
on our face.

00:03:56.135 --> 00:03:57.904 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
[ Laughs ]

00:03:57.904 --> 00:04:02.008 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I'll let you guys decide
which body part.

00:04:02.008 --> 00:04:03.042 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
This is amazing.

00:04:03.042 --> 00:04:05.111 align:start size:94% position:6%
You were at NYU.
-Mm-hmm.

00:04:05.111 --> 00:04:08.348
-And the day you -- Was it the
day you took your last test,

00:04:08.348 --> 00:04:10.783 line:92%
you got cast in a soap opera?

00:04:10.783 --> 00:04:12.952 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-Wow! That's incredible.

00:04:12.952 --> 00:04:16.089 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I took my last exam
for college,

00:04:16.089 --> 00:04:18.658
and it was, like,
anatomy or something really hard

00:04:18.658 --> 00:04:21.094 size:78% position:39%
that I was not sure I
was going to pass.

00:04:21.094 --> 00:04:22.395 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-But then I did.

00:04:22.395 --> 00:04:24.731 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I walked out
and called my parents.

00:04:24.731 --> 00:04:28.001
And I was like, "I'm a graduate.
This is amazing."

00:04:28.001 --> 00:04:29.769 align:start size:94% position:6%
And four hours later,
I got the call

00:04:29.769 --> 00:04:32.272
that I'd booked a four-year
contract on "One Life to Live."

00:04:32.272 --> 00:04:35.141 size:84% position:42%
-Wow! That's amazing.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:35.141 --> 00:04:39.979 align:start size:94% position:6%
They were probably
just waiting to see

00:04:39.979 --> 00:04:42.181 align:start size:94% position:6%
how you did on that
anatomy test.

00:04:42.181 --> 00:04:42.715 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Yeah, yeah.

00:04:42.715 --> 00:04:44.150 align:start size:94% position:6%
They probably had a plant
in the room,

00:04:44.150 --> 00:04:46.419 align:start size:94% position:6%
just like, "Looks like she
knows the answers."

00:04:46.419 --> 00:04:47.553 size:78% position:39%
-"She's going to have
the grades, guys."

00:04:47.553 --> 00:04:50.990
-"She's gonna have the grades.
She's not gonna have to stay."

00:04:50.990 --> 00:04:54.027 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Well, thank you so much
for being here.

